items.doc:
Make a root generator from a world seed.

```
let mut r = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(1);
let _ = r.next_u64();
```

The fixed key of this generator. Sub-streams hash this key.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
assert_eq!(Rng::new(3).key(), Rng::new(3).key());
```

A named sub-stream. It depends only on this generator's key and
`name`. Draws from the parent do not change it.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let mut world = Rng::new(9);
let before = world.stream("kelp").next_u64();
world.next_u64();
assert_eq!(world.stream("kelp").next_u64(), before);
```

A named, numbered sub-stream: one per chunk, per level, per wave.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let world = Rng::new(9);
let mut chunk_3 = world.stream_n("chunk", 3);
let _ = chunk_3.f32();
```

A float in `[0, 1)`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).f32();
assert!((0.0..1.0).contains(&v));
```

A float in `[lo, hi)`. If `hi <= lo`, the result is `lo`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).range(2.0, 4.0);
assert!((2.0..4.0).contains(&v));
```

An integer in `[lo, hi)`. If `hi <= lo`, the result is `lo`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).range_i(0, 6);
assert!((0..6).contains(&v));
```

An index in `[0, len)`. If `len` is 0, the result is 0.

```
let i = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).index(3);
assert!(i < 3);
```

One item of a slice, or `None` if the slice is empty.

```
let names = ["kelp", "coral"];
assert!(warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).pick(&names).is_some());
```

Shuffle a slice in place (Fisher-Yates).

```
let mut v = [1, 2, 3, 4];
warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).shuffle(&mut v);
```

A unit vector in a random direction.

```
let d = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).unit_vec2();
assert!(((d[0] * d[0] + d[1] * d[1]) - 1.0).abs() < 1e-4);
```

A point in a disc of this radius round `center`, with even density.

```
let p = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).in_disc([0.0, 0.0], 2.0);
assert!(p[0].hypot(p[1]) <= 2.0);
```

