What the status line shows.

```ignore
use warp_sdk::boot::{Splash, Status};
Splash::new("REEF").status(Status::words(["Waking the reef", "Lighting the water"])).install();
```

True while a request waits for the render loop.

```ignore
warp_core::shot::request(None);
assert!(warp_core::shot::pending());
```

Capture the next frame of the primary viewport as a PNG.

`None` writes to `screenshots_dir()` with a time-stamped name. `Some(p)`
writes to `p` and makes its parent folders. A relative `p` starts at the
working folder of the process.

```ignore
// In Renderer::render, look at frame 120 of the game:
if self.frame == 120 {
warp_core::shot::request(Some("target/shots/title.png".into()));
}
```

