items.doc:
The player as the arena sees it.

```
use warp_sdk::challenge::{Player, Tool};
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let p = Player::new(Vec2::zero(), 100.0).with_tool(Tool::dart());
assert_eq!(p.loadout.slots.len(), 1);
```

The fixed key of this generator. Sub-streams hash this key.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
assert_eq!(Rng::new(3).key(), Rng::new(3).key());
```

A named sub-stream. It depends only on this generator's key and
`name`. Draws from the parent do not change it.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let mut world = Rng::new(9);
let before = world.stream("kelp").next_u64();
world.next_u64();
assert_eq!(world.stream("kelp").next_u64(), before);
```

A named, numbered sub-stream: one per chunk, per level, per wave.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let world = Rng::new(9);
let mut chunk_3 = world.stream_n("chunk", 3);
let _ = chunk_3.f32();
```

A float in `[0, 1)`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).f32();
assert!((0.0..1.0).contains(&v));
```

An integer in `[lo, hi)`. If `hi <= lo`, the result is `lo`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).range_i(0, 6);
assert!((0..6).contains(&v));
```

An index in `[0, len)`. If `len` is 0, the result is 0.

```
let i = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).index(3);
assert!(i < 3);
```

One item of a slice, or `None` if the slice is empty.

```
let names = ["kelp", "coral"];
assert!(warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).pick(&names).is_some());
```

Shuffle a slice in place (Fisher-Yates).

```
let mut v = [1, 2, 3, 4];
warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).shuffle(&mut v);
```

A unit vector in a random direction.

```
let d = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).unit_vec2();
assert!(((d[0] * d[0] + d[1] * d[1]) - 1.0).abs() < 1e-4);
```

A point in a disc of this radius round `center`, with even density.

```
let p = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).in_disc([0.0, 0.0], 2.0);
assert!(p[0].hypot(p[1]) <= 2.0);
```

A shot to `point` with the default timing.

```
use warp_sdk::camera::Shot;
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::new(5.0, 0.0));
assert!(shot.scale.is_none());
```

Set the zoom scale at the point.

```
# use warp_sdk::camera::Shot; use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::zero()).zoom(2.0);
```

Set the seconds of the pan to the point and of the pan back.

```
# use warp_sdk::camera::Shot; use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::zero()).travel(1.5, 1.0);
```

Set the seconds at the point.

```
# use warp_sdk::camera::Shot; use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::zero()).hold(3.0);
```

Show letterbox bars of this fraction of the screen height. A value
of 0.1 is a good cinematic look.

```
# use warp_sdk::camera::Shot; use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::zero()).letterbox(0.1);
```

The full length of the shot in seconds.

```
# use warp_sdk::camera::Shot; use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
assert!(Shot::to(Vec2::zero()).duration() > 0.0);
```

A critically damped spring: the fastest move to a target with no
overshoot. Use it for a value whose target changes at any time, such as
a hover amount or a cursor follower.

The step is the exact solution, so ten steps of 1/600 s land where one
step of 1/60 s lands. The result does not change with the frame rate.

```ignore
let mut s = cine::Spring::new(0.0).settle_secs(0.25);
s.target = 1.0;
s.step(dt);
let amount = s.value;
```

