/// A straight edge that crosses the screen in one direction.
Linear(Dir),
/// A circle that grows from the centre, then a hole that grows after it.
Radial,
/// A hand that sweeps once round from twelve o'clock.
Clock,

/// Instant change. WHEN: the action continues, and the player must not
/// wait. The default of film and of menus: a submenu, a tab, a list.
Cut,
/// Fade down to black, then up on the new screen. WHEN: time passes, a
/// chapter ends, the player dies or respawns, a level loads.
DipToBlack,
/// Fade through one colour. WHEN: a flash of impact or memory (white),
/// damage or alarm (red), a power-up (the accent colour).
DipToColor(Color32),
/// The old screen fades out as the new fades in. WHEN: the same place at
/// another time, or one layer over another, such as pause over play.
Crossfade,
/// Both screens move together, side by side. WHEN: the screens are
/// neighbours in space. Push left to go forward, push right to go back,
/// push up to go to a deeper level.
Push(Dir),
/// The new screen slides over the old one, which stays still. WHEN: a
/// card on top of the table: a modal panel, an inventory, a dialog.
Slide(Dir),
/// A shape closes on one point, then opens on the new screen. WHEN: the
/// scene ends on one subject that matters. `at: None` is the centre.
Iris { shape: IrisShape, at: Option<Pos2> },
/// An edge crosses the screen. WHEN: a change of place or of story line.
/// The clock wipe says that time passes.
Wipe(WipeShape),
/// The camera moves into the old screen and through it. WHEN: the
/// player goes deeper: menu into level, world map into region.
DollyThrough,
/// The focus moves from one plane to the next in the same space. WHEN:
/// the attention changes and the place does not. The world goes soft
/// as the menu over it comes sharp. See [`Cine::blur`].
RackFocus,
/// One shape becomes the next. WHEN: continuity of a thing. The button
/// the player pressed grows into the panel it opens. `from` and `to`
/// are screen rects.
MatchCut { from: Rect, to: Rect },
/// The old screen breaks into cells that close, then open on the new
/// screen. WHEN: a dream, a teleport, a signal lost, a thing that decays.
NoiseDissolve,

/// Progress below one half: the old screen leads.
Out,
/// Progress at or above one half: the new screen leads.
In,
/// Progress at one. The transition is over.
Done,

