items.doc:
The title screen: wordmark and Continue, New game, Load, Settings, Quit.

Keep one `Title` in the game state and call [`Title::show`] each frame
while the title is up. "New game" is always present. "Continue" is
present only while `has_save` is true, and it is first when present.

```ignore
let mut title = Title::new("REEF").tagline("a living sea").layout(Layout::LeftRail);
title.has_save = slots.latest().is_some();
if let Some(a) = title.show(ctx) { handle(a); }
```

The pause screen: Resume, Settings, Save, Load, Quit to title, Quit.
Escape gives `Resume`. "Resume" and "Quit to title" are always present.

```ignore
let mut pause = Pause::new().layout(Layout::LeftRail);
match pause.show(ctx) {
Some(MenuAction::Resume) => state = Play,
Some(MenuAction::Save) => { slots.write(1, &meta, &data).ok(); }
_ => {}
}
```

