The rule helper. Call it right after a forced change of state. In a debug
build it panics when no cue of `kind` reached the global state in the
last second. A release build does nothing.

```ignore
fn respawn(&mut self) {
let old = self.pos;
self.pos = self.spawn;
cues::emit(Cue::new(Kind::Respawn, self.pos).from(old));
cues::debug_assert_cued(Kind::Respawn);
}
```

