items.doc:
Add a reward.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").reward(Reward::resource("ore", 1.0));
```

Add a cost: a hazard and its rate per second.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").cost(Hazard::Toxicity, 0.3);
```

Set the drag. 1 is open water.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").drag(3.0);
```

Set the current, in world units per second.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").current(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(0.0, -1.0));
```

Set the ambient light, 0..1.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").light(0.2);
```

Add a spawn table entry.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").spawn(Spawn { id: "crab".into(), weight: 2.0, max: 6 });
```

Set the ambience tag.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").ambience("drip_cave");
```

Set the palette shift.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").palette(PaletteShift { hue: 0.1, saturation: 1.2, value: 0.8 });
```

Set the particle mood.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").particles(ParticleMood::Murky);
```

Set the fog colour (linear RGB) and density (0..1).

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").fog([0.1, 0.3, 0.1], 0.6);
```

Place the biome in the band `[lo, hi]` on the `p.y` axis.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let _ = Biome::new("a").band(10.0, 50.0);
```

Finish a biome. Refuses a biome with no reward or no cost, so a biome
always differs from the default biome in play, not only in looks.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let ok = Biome::new("a").reward(Reward::resource("x", 1.0)).cost(Hazard::Heat, 0.1).build();
assert!(ok.is_ok());
```

Finish the default biome. It needs no reward and no cost.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let base = Biome::base("open").light(1.0).build_base();
```

A problem that [`BiomeSet::check`] found.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::BiomeIssue;
let i = BiomeIssue::LooksOnly { a: 1, b: 2 };
```

items.body:
/// Biomes `a` and `b` play the same. Only their looks differ.
LooksOnly { a: usize, b: usize },
