items.doc:
The two strongest biomes at a point and the share of the second.

Mix any value as `a * (1 - t) + b * t`, with `a` from `primary` and
`b` from `secondary`. `t` is in `0..=0.5`.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::Blend;
let b = Blend { primary: 1, secondary: 0, t: 0.25 };
assert_eq!(b.mix(10.0, 20.0), 12.5);
```

Mix a primary value and a secondary value by `t`.

```
let b = warp_sdk::world::biome::Blend { primary: 0, secondary: 0, t: 0.0 };
assert_eq!(b.mix(3.0, 9.0), 3.0);
```

The blended gameplay and looks at one point. Feed it to the player's
physics, damage, light and post settings each frame.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::{Biome, BiomeSet, Hazard};
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 1);
let env = set.env(Vec2::new(0.0, 0.0));
assert_eq!(env.hazard(Hazard::Heat), 0.0);
let v = env.movement.apply(Vec2::new(1.0, 0.0), 1.0 / 60.0);
```

The blended rate of one hazard.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
# let env = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).env(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero());
let heat = env.hazard(Hazard::Heat);
```

All biomes of a world, the base biome at index 0, and the placement noise.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::{Biome, BiomeSet, Hazard, Reward};
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 42)
.feather(6.0)
.border_noise(8.0, 40.0)
.with(Biome::new("deep").reward(Reward::discovery("wreck")).cost(Hazard::Darkness, 0.2)
.band(50.0, 200.0).build().unwrap());
assert_eq!(set.len(), 2);
```

A set with only the base biome. Defaults: feather 4, border noise
amplitude 6 and scale 32 world units.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 3);
```

Add a biome. Its index is the order of the `with` calls, from 1.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let b = Biome::new("x").reward(Reward::resource("r", 1.0)).cost(Hazard::Heat, 1.0).build().unwrap();
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).with(b);
```

Set the width of the soft border, in band units.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).feather(10.0);
```

Set how far the noise moves a border (`amplitude`) and the size of
its waves (`scale`), in world units. Amplitude 0 = straight borders.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).border_noise(0.0, 1.0);
```

The number of biomes, the base biome included.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
assert_eq!(BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).len(), 1);
```

Always false: a set holds at least the base biome.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
assert!(!BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).is_empty());
```

One biome by index. Index 0 is the base biome.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 0);
assert_eq!(set.biome(0).name, "open");
```

All biomes, the base biome first.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 0);
for b in set.biomes() { let _ = &b.name; }
```

Find each pair of biomes that play the same and each biome that adds
no reward or no cost to the base biome. `Ok` when there is none.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let a = Biome::new("a").reward(Reward::resource("r", 1.0)).cost(Hazard::Heat, 1.0).build().unwrap();
let mut b = a.clone();
b.name = "b".into();
b.looks.fog = [1.0, 0.0, 0.0];
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0).with(a).with(b);
assert_eq!(set.check(), Err(vec![BiomeIssue::LooksOnly { a: 1, b: 2 }]));
```

The membership of every biome at `p`, the base biome first.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0);
assert_eq!(set.weights(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero()), vec![1.0]);
```

The two strongest biomes at `p` and the share `t` of the second.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0);
let b = set.sample(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(5.0, 5.0));
assert_eq!((b.primary, b.t), (0, 0.0));
```

The blended gameplay and looks at `p`.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").light(0.8).build_base(), 0);
assert!((set.env(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero()).light - 0.8).abs() < 1e-6);
```

The event that [`BiomeTracker::update`] returns on the first entry to a
biome.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::Discovered;
let d = Discovered { biome: 2 };
```

Remembers which biomes the player has entered and which one they are in.

```
use warp_sdk::world::biome::{Biome, BiomeSet, BiomeTracker, Discovered};
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("open").build_base(), 0);
let mut t = BiomeTracker::new(&set);
assert_eq!(t.update(&set, Vec2::zero()), Some(Discovered { biome: 0 }));
assert_eq!(t.update(&set, Vec2::zero()), None);
```

A tracker with no biome seen.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
let t = BiomeTracker::new(&BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0));
```

Call once per frame with the player position. Returns
[`Discovered`] the first time the primary biome at `p` is new.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
# let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0);
let mut t = BiomeTracker::new(&set);
if let Some(d) = t.update(&set, warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero()) { let _ = d.biome; }
```

The biome the player was in at the last `update`.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
# let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0);
assert_eq!(BiomeTracker::new(&set).current(), None);
```

True when the player has entered biome `i` at least once.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::biome::*;
# let set = BiomeSet::new(Biome::base("o").build_base(), 0);
assert!(!BiomeTracker::new(&set).has_seen(0));
```

