items.doc:
A light. Default feather is a quarter of the radius, skin 0.

```
let s = warp_sdk::world::reveal::Source::light(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 8.0);
assert_eq!(s.feather, 2.0);
```

Why [`RevealGrid::from_bytes`] refused the data.

```
use warp_sdk::world::reveal::{RevealGrid, RevealError};
assert_eq!(RevealGrid::from_bytes(b"nope").unwrap_err(), RevealError::BadMagic);
```

items.body:
/// The data does not start with the reveal grid tag.
BadMagic,
/// The data stops before the grid is complete, or has more data.
BadLength,
/// The header has a size of 0 or a cell size that is not positive.
BadHeader,

items.doc:
The exploration grid. Row-major, row 0 at `origin.y`.

```
use warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid;
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let grid = RevealGrid::new(Vec2::new(-100.0, 0.0), 2.0, 100, 50);
assert_eq!(grid.size(), (100, 50));
```

The size in cells.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 4);
assert_eq!(g.size(), (8, 4));
```

The world size of one cell.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 0.5, 8, 4);
assert_eq!(g.cell_size(), 0.5);
```

The world rectangle `[x, y, width, height]`.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 2.0, 8, 4);
assert_eq!(g.rect(), [0.0, 0.0, 16.0, 8.0]);
```

`[x, y, 1/width, 1/height]` for the shader: `uv = (p - r.xy) * r.zw`.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 2.0, 8, 4);
assert_eq!(g.uv_rect(), [0.0, 0.0, 1.0 / 16.0, 1.0 / 8.0]);
```

A number that changes each time the grid changes. Use it to skip
work when nothing changed.

```
# let mut g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
let r = g.revision();
g.clear();
assert_ne!(g.revision(), r);
```

Clear `visible`. Call it once per frame before the `reveal` calls.

```
# let mut g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
g.begin_frame();
```

Clear `explored` and `visible`: a new map.

```
# let mut g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
g.clear();
```

The centre of cell `(cx, cy)` in world units.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 2.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.cell_centre(0, 0), warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0));
```

The cell that holds `p`, or `None` outside the grid.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 2.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.cell_of(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(3.0, 1.0)), Some((1, 0)));
```

The `(explored, visible)` values of one cell, 0..1. Outside = `(0, 0)`.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.cell(2, 3), (0.0, 0.0));
```

The explored value at `p`, bilinear between cell centres.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.explored_at(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(4.0, 4.0)), 0.0);
```

The visible-now value at `p`, bilinear between cell centres.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.visible_at(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::new(4.0, 4.0)), 0.0);
```

Reveal the cells that `src` reaches and has line of sight to.
`solid(p)` is true where `p` is rock or wall. Values only go up:
several sources in one frame keep the brightest value.

The cost is one `solid` call per half cell along each ray, for each
cell in the radius. A radius of 20 cells is about 25 000 calls.

```
use warp_sdk::world::reveal::{RevealGrid, Source};
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let mut g = RevealGrid::new(Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 32, 32);
g.reveal(&Source::sonar(Vec2::new(16.0, 16.0), 10.0), |_| false);
assert!(g.explored_at(Vec2::new(16.0, 16.0)) > 0.9);
assert_eq!(g.visible_at(Vec2::new(16.0, 16.0)), 0.0);
```

One RGBA pixel per cell, row 0 first, for a minimap. Each pixel mixes
`unknown`, `remembered` and `seen` by the cell values.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
let rgba = g.minimap_rgba([0, 0, 0, 255], [60, 70, 80, 255], [200, 220, 255, 255]);
assert_eq!(rgba.len(), 8 * 8 * 4);
```

The explored values, one byte per cell, row 0 first. This is the
data of the `explored` R8 texture.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.explored_r8().len(), 64);
```

The visible-now values, one byte per cell, row 0 first.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
assert_eq!(g.visible_r8().len(), 64);
```

Save the grid. `visible` is not saved: it is for one frame only.
The explored values are run-length coded, so a large dark map is small.

```
# let g = warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 64, 64);
assert!(g.to_bytes().len() < 64);
```

Load a grid that [`RevealGrid::to_bytes`] saved. `visible` is clear.

```
# use warp_sdk::world::reveal::RevealGrid;
# let g = RevealGrid::new(warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2::zero(), 1.0, 8, 8);
let back = RevealGrid::from_bytes(&g.to_bytes()).unwrap();
assert_eq!(back.size(), (8, 8));
```

The two `R8Unorm` textures of a grid on the GPU, for
`shaderlib/terrain/reveal.wgsl`. Bind both views with a linear sampler
and pass [`RevealGrid::uv_rect`] in a uniform.

```ignore
let mut gpu = RevealGpu::new(&device, &grid);
// each frame, after the reveal calls:
gpu.upload(&queue, &grid);
let rect: [f32; 4] = grid.uv_rect();
```

