The world: a chunked density grid with an exact surface.

```ignore
let mut t = Terrain::generate(TerrainConfig::side(3));
if t.sdf(p) < 0.0 { /* p is inside rock */ }
t.dig(p, 2.0);
```

Make a world from a field. `f(p)` is about the signed distance to the
surface in world units, POSITIVE inside solid. Each node gets `mat::ROCK`.

```ignore
let c = Vec2::new(16.0, 16.0);
let t = Terrain::from_fn(TerrainConfig::side(0), |p| 5.0 - (p - c).mag());
```

The SDF as an R16Float texture, and its world rect
`[min_x, min_y, size_x, size_y]`. The first call makes the texture.
Later calls re-bake the dirty chunks only.

```ignore
let (view, rect) = terrain.sdf_texture(&device, &queue);
// WGSL: let d = textureSample(sdf, samp, (p - rect.xy) / rect.zw).r;
```

Move `current` to `target` with a critically damped spring.

`velocity` is the spring state. Keep it between calls. `smooth_time` is
about the time in seconds to reach the target. The result never moves
past a still target. This is the spring that the camera uses.

```
use warp_sdk::camera::smooth_damp;
let (mut x, mut v) = (0.0_f32, 0.0_f32);
for _ in 0..120 { x = smooth_damp(x, 10.0, &mut v, 0.2, 1.0 / 60.0); }
assert!((x - 10.0).abs() < 0.01);
```

How the camera follows its target. All lengths are view units (see the
module header).

```
use warp_sdk::camera::{Camera2d, Follow};
let mut cam = Camera2d::new([1280, 720]);
cam.follow = Follow { look_ahead: 0.0, ..Follow::default() };
```

items.body:
/// About the time in seconds that the rig takes to reach the aim point.
/// Small values feel tight, large values feel heavy. Default 0.25.
pub smooth_time: f32,
/// Seconds of target velocity that the camera looks ahead. Default 0.3.
pub look_ahead: f32,
/// The longest look-ahead, view units. Default 0.35.
pub look_ahead_max: f32,
/// The damping time of the look-ahead, seconds. A turn then does not
/// whip the camera. Default 0.5.
pub look_ahead_smooth: f32,
/// Half extents of the dead zone, view units. The rig does not move
/// while the aim point is inside it. Default `[0.12, 0.08]`.
pub dead_zone: [f32; 2],
/// Half extents of the soft zone, view units. The target never leaves
/// it: the rig moves hard at its edge. Zero or less turns the limit off.
/// Default `[0.6, 0.5]`.
pub soft_zone: [f32; 2],

/// The largest translation, view units. Default 0.06.
pub max_offset: f32,
/// The largest rotation, radians. Default 0.05.
pub max_angle: f32,
/// The noise speed, in noise cells per second. Default 15.
pub frequency: f32,
/// Trauma lost per second. Default 1.2.
pub decay: f32,
/// The reduce-motion scale, 0 to 1. 0 turns shake off, 1 is full shake.
/// Connect it to the accessibility setting of the game. Default 1.
pub motion_scale: f32,

