Bounds from two corners in any order.

```
use warp_sdk::camera::Bounds;
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let b = Bounds::new(Vec2::new(4.0, 1.0), Vec2::new(-4.0, -1.0));
assert_eq!(b.min, Vec2::new(-4.0, -1.0));
```

Clamp a view centre so that a view of `half` extents stays inside.

```
use warp_sdk::camera::Bounds;
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let b = Bounds::new(Vec2::new(0.0, 0.0), Vec2::new(10.0, 10.0));
let c = b.clamp_center(Vec2::new(-5.0, 5.0), Vec2::new(2.0, 2.0));
assert_eq!(c, Vec2::new(2.0, 5.0));
```

A cinematic move: pan to a point of interest, hold, then return to the
follow target. Build it with [`Shot::to`] and the setters.

```
use warp_sdk::camera::Shot;
use warp_sdk::ultraviolet::Vec2;
let shot = Shot::to(Vec2::new(30.0, 4.0)).zoom(3.0).hold(2.0).letterbox(0.1);
assert_eq!(shot.duration(), shot.travel + 2.0 + shot.back);
```

