items.doc:
Makes a kind with size 1.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::{ResourceId, ResourceKind, Role};
let food = ResourceKind::new(ResourceId(0), "food", "icon.food", Role::Food);
assert_eq!(food.size, 1);
```

Sets the space that one item takes. A value of 0 becomes 0: the item
then takes no space (for example, a currency).

```
use warp_sdk::economy::{ResourceId, ResourceKind, Role};
let coin = ResourceKind::new(ResourceId(9), "coin", "icon.coin", Role::Currency).size(0);
assert_eq!(coin.size, 0);
```

The list of resource kinds that a game uses.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut cat = Catalog::new();
cat.add(ResourceKind::new(ResourceId(0), "food", "icon.food", Role::Food));
assert_eq!(cat.get(ResourceId(0)).unwrap().name, "food");
```

The space that one item takes. An unknown id takes 1.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
assert_eq!(Catalog::new().size_of(ResourceId(7)), 1);
```

All kinds with one role, in id order.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut cat = Catalog::new();
cat.add(ResourceKind::new(ResourceId(0), "food", "i", Role::Food));
assert_eq!(cat.with_role(Role::Food).count(), 1);
```

A list of resource amounts. A cost, the inputs of a recipe and the
outputs of a recipe are all bundles.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let cost = Bundle::new().with(ResourceId(0), 5).with(ResourceId(1), 2);
assert_eq!(cost.get(ResourceId(1)), 2);
```

A container with a capacity: the cargo hold of a submarine, the storage
of a base, the stomach of a colony.

The capacity is in space units. Each item takes [`ResourceKind::size`]
units. A store can also have a limit per kind.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let hold = Store::new("cargo", 20).limit(ResourceId(0), 5);
assert_eq!(hold.capacity, 20);
```

