items.doc:
In minus out.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::Rate;
assert_eq!(Rate { in_per_s: 2.0, out_per_s: 0.5 }.net(), 1.5);
```

A record of recent changes, for HUD number pops and measured rates.

Small changes with the same store, id, cause and sign that come close
together merge into one entry. So a flow that adds 1 item each frame
shows as one growing "+12", not as twelve "+1" pops.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut eco = Economy::new(Catalog::new());
let s = eco.add_store(Store::new("s", 10));
eco.add(s, ResourceId(0), 3);
let pop = eco.ledger().recent(1.0).next().unwrap();
assert_eq!(pop.delta, 3);
```

