items.doc:
All stores, flows and craft jobs of a game, with one clock and one ledger.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut eco = Economy::new(Catalog::new());
let hold = eco.add_store(Store::new("cargo", 4));
assert_eq!(eco.add(hold, ResourceId(0), 9), 4);
```

Sets the capacity of a store (for example, after a cargo upgrade).
Items over a smaller capacity stay; new items do not go in until
there is room.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut eco = Economy::new(Catalog::new());
let hold = eco.add_store(Store::new("cargo", 4));
eco.set_capacity(hold, 8);
assert_eq!(eco.store(hold).unwrap().free(), 8);
```

Moves up to `n` items of `res` from `from` to `to`. A partial fill
moves what fits and leaves the rest in `from`. Gives the number moved.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut eco = Economy::new(Catalog::new());
let a = eco.add_store(Store::new("cargo", 10));
let b = eco.add_store(Store::new("base", 3));
eco.add(a, ResourceId(0), 5);
assert_eq!(eco.transfer(a, b, ResourceId(0), 5), 3);
assert_eq!(eco.amount(a, ResourceId(0)), 2);
```

What `store` still needs to afford `cost`. Empty when it can pay.
The HUD can draw these amounts in red beside the upgrade.

```
use warp_sdk::economy::*;
let mut eco = Economy::new(Catalog::new());
let base = eco.add_store(Store::new("base", 10));
eco.add(base, ResourceId(0), 2);
let need = eco.missing(base, &Bundle::new().with(ResourceId(0), 5));
