```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Node};
let m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().node(Node::new("a")));
assert!(m.can_buy("a").is_ok());
```

Buys a node: checks the prerequisites, removes the cost from the
wallet one time, and unlocks the node. On an error the state does not
change.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Node};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().node(Node::new("a").cost("shells", 3)));
m.earn("shells", 5);
m.buy("a").unwrap();
assert_eq!(m.balance("shells"), 2);
```

The level of an upgrade. 0 means not bought.

```
let m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
assert_eq!(m.upgrade_level("hull"), 0);
```

The cost of the next level of an upgrade, as (currency, amount).
`None` if the upgrade is unknown or at its maximum level.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Upgrade};
let m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().upgrade(Upgrade::new("hull").costs(&[4, 9])));
assert_eq!(m.next_upgrade_cost("hull"), Some(("points".to_string(), 4)));
```

Buys the next level of an upgrade. The cost leaves the wallet one
time. On an error the state does not change.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Upgrade};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().upgrade(Upgrade::new("hull").costs(&[4])));
m.earn("points", 4);
assert_eq!(m.buy_upgrade("hull"), Ok(1));
```

Records one observation of a codex entry. The first observation of
an entry sends `Discovered` with `Seen`. Each later change of state
sends `Discovered` again. Returns the state after the observation.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Knowledge};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new());
assert_eq!(m.observe("fish", "lantern"), Knowledge::Seen);
```

The knowledge state of a codex entry.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Knowledge};
let m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new());
assert_eq!(m.knowledge("fish", "lantern"), Knowledge::Unseen);
```

The entries of one codex kind with their states, sorted by id.
Unseen entries are not in the list, because the codex does not know
them.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new());
m.observe("fish", "eel");
assert_eq!(m.codex_entries("fish").len(), 1);
```

Every active effect id: the effects of unlocked nodes, then each
upgrade effect one time per level. The game applies them.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Upgrade};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().upgrade(Upgrade::new("hull").costs(&[0, 0]).effect("hp+10")));
m.buy_upgrade("hull").unwrap();
m.buy_upgrade("hull").unwrap();
assert_eq!(m.effects(), vec!["hp+10".to_string(), "hp+10".to_string()]);
```

How many times an effect id is active. Use it for stacked bonuses.

```
let m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
assert_eq!(m.effect_count("hp+10"), 0);
```

The fraction (0 to 1) of the way to a stage. A fired stage gives 1.
An unknown stage gives 0. Use it for a HUD bar.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Stage};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().stage(Stage::new("s", "polyps", 4)));
m.count("polyps", 1);
assert_eq!(m.stage_progress("s"), 0.25);
```

The next stage that has not fired, in design order. `None` when every
stage fired. Use it to show the player the next goal.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Stage};
let m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().stage(Stage::new("s", "polyps", 4)));
assert_eq!(m.next_stage().map(|s| s.id.as_str()), Some("s"));
```

The fraction (0 to 1) of the way to a milestone: the lowest fraction
of its conditions. A fired milestone gives 1.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, Milestone};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new().milestone(Milestone::new("m").when("x", 2)));
m.count("x", 1);
assert_eq!(m.milestone_progress("m"), 0.5);
```

True if the milestone fired.

```
let m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
assert!(!m.has_milestone("m"));
```

True if the stage fired.

```
let m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
assert!(!m.has_stage("s"));
```

Starts a new run: sets every counter whose name starts with `run.` to
zero and adds one to [`Progress::runs`]. All other state stays.

```
let mut m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
m.count("run.depth", 5);
m.count("dives", 1);
m.begin_run();
assert_eq!((m.counter("run.depth"), m.counter("dives")), (0, 1));
```

Takes all events since the last call, oldest first.

```
let mut m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
m.observe("fish", "eel");
assert_eq!(m.drain_events().len(), 1);
assert!(m.drain_events().is_empty());
```

Writes the state to versioned bytes. The design is not in the bytes.

```
let m = warp_sdk::metaprog::Meta::new(warp_sdk::metaprog::MetaDef::new());
assert_eq!(&m.save()[..4], b"WMP\0");
```

Reads a state from bytes that [`Meta::save`] wrote, and joins it to a
design. Stages and milestones that the old state did not reach, but
now holds, fire after the load.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef};
let mut m = Meta::new(MetaDef::new());
m.earn("shells", 3);
let back = Meta::load(MetaDef::new(), &m.save()).unwrap();
assert_eq!(back.balance("shells"), 3);
```

Why [`Meta::load`] refused the bytes.

```
use warp_sdk::metaprog::{Meta, MetaDef, LoadError};
assert_eq!(Meta::load(MetaDef::new(), b"xx").unwrap_err(), LoadError::BadMagic);
```

