items.doc:
A deterministic random number generator (xoshiro256**).

The same seed gives the same numbers on every machine and every run.
`stream` and `stream_n` give sub-streams that depend only on this
generator's key and the name, not on the numbers it already gave.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let world = Rng::new(7);
let mut fish = world.stream("fish");
let x = fish.range(0.0, 10.0);
assert!((0.0..10.0).contains(&x));
assert_eq!(Rng::new(7).stream("fish").next_u64(), Rng::new(7).stream("fish").next_u64());
```

Make a root generator from a world seed.

```
let mut r = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(1);
let _ = r.next_u64();
```

The fixed key of this generator. Sub-streams hash this key.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
assert_eq!(Rng::new(3).key(), Rng::new(3).key());
```

A named sub-stream. It depends only on this generator's key and
`name`. Draws from the parent do not change it.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let mut world = Rng::new(9);
let before = world.stream("kelp").next_u64();
world.next_u64();
assert_eq!(world.stream("kelp").next_u64(), before);
```

A named, numbered sub-stream: one per chunk, per level, per wave.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rng;
let world = Rng::new(9);
let mut chunk_3 = world.stream_n("chunk", 3);
let _ = chunk_3.f32();
```

A float in `[0, 1)`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).f32();
assert!((0.0..1.0).contains(&v));
```

A float in `[lo, hi)`. If `hi <= lo`, the result is `lo`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).range(2.0, 4.0);
assert!((2.0..4.0).contains(&v));
```

An integer in `[lo, hi)`. If `hi <= lo`, the result is `lo`.

```
let v = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).range_i(0, 6);
assert!((0..6).contains(&v));
```

An index in `[0, len)`. If `len` is 0, the result is 0.

```
let i = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).index(3);
assert!(i < 3);
```

One item of a slice, or `None` if the slice is empty.

```
let names = ["kelp", "coral"];
assert!(warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).pick(&names).is_some());
```

Shuffle a slice in place (Fisher-Yates).

```
let mut v = [1, 2, 3, 4];
warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).shuffle(&mut v);
```

A unit vector in a random direction.

```
let d = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).unit_vec2();
assert!(((d[0] * d[0] + d[1] * d[1]) - 1.0).abs() < 1e-4);
```

A point in a disc of this radius round `center`, with even density.

```
let p = warp_sdk::procgen::Rng::new(0).in_disc([0.0, 0.0], 2.0);
assert!(p[0].hypot(p[1]) <= 2.0);
```

An axis-aligned rectangle: `min` is inclusive, `max` is exclusive.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Area;
let a = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [10.0, 5.0]);
assert!(a.contains([1.0, 1.0]));
```

Make an area from two corners in any order.

```
let a = warp_sdk::procgen::Area::new([4.0, 4.0], [0.0, 0.0]);
assert_eq!(a.min, [0.0, 0.0]);
```

A random point in the area.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{Area, Rng};
let a = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [1.0, 1.0]);
assert!(a.contains(a.random_point(&mut Rng::new(0))));
```

One Poisson-disc point and the radius that kept other points away.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{poisson_disc_density, Area, Rng};
let s = poisson_disc_density(&mut Rng::new(1), Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [20.0, 20.0]), 1.0, 3.0, |_| 1.0);
assert!(s.iter().all(|s| s.radius == 1.0));
```

Even Poisson-disc points: no two points are closer than `radius`.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{poisson_disc, Area, Rng};
let pts = poisson_disc(&mut Rng::new(5), Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [50.0, 50.0]), 4.0);
assert!(pts.len() > 20);
```

Poisson-disc points from a density map.

`density(p)` returns a value in `[0, 1]`. At 1 the spacing is `r_min`; at
values near 0 the spacing goes to `r_max`. At 0 or less the area has no
points. Two points `a` and `b` are never closer than the larger of their
two radii.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{poisson_disc_density, Area, Rng};
let area = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [40.0, 40.0]);
// Dense at the bottom, empty above y = 30.
let pts = poisson_disc_density(&mut Rng::new(2), area, 1.0, 4.0, |p| 1.0 - p[1] / 30.0);
assert!(pts.iter().all(|s| s.pos[1] < 30.0));
```

Poisson-disc points with a radius closure.

`radius(p)` returns the spacing at `p`, or `None` where no point may go.
The result is clamped to `[r_min, r_max]`. Two points are never closer
than the larger of their two radii. Zero-radius gaps do not stop the
fill: when the front stops, random throws look for new free space.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{poisson_disc_variable, Area, Rng};
let area = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [30.0, 30.0]);
let pts = poisson_disc_variable(&mut Rng::new(3), area, 1.0, 3.0, |p| {
if p[0] < 15.0 { Some(1.0) } else { Some(3.0) }
});
assert!(!pts.is_empty());
```

A list of items with weights. `pick` returns one item; an item with a
larger weight comes back more often. Weights of 0 or less never come back.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{Rng, WeightedTable};
let table = WeightedTable::new()
.with("brain coral", 3.0)
.with("fan coral", 2.0)
.with("giant clam", 0.2);
let kind = table.pick(&mut Rng::new(4)).unwrap();
assert!(["brain coral", "fan coral", "giant clam"].contains(kind));
```

An empty table.

```
let t: warp_sdk::procgen::WeightedTable<u8> = warp_sdk::procgen::WeightedTable::new();
assert!(t.is_empty());
```

Add an item and return the table (builder form).

```
let t = warp_sdk::procgen::WeightedTable::new().with('a', 1.0);
assert_eq!(t.len(), 1);
```

Add an item.

```
let mut t = warp_sdk::procgen::WeightedTable::new();
t.push('a', 2.0);
assert_eq!(t.total(), 2.0);
```

The index of one item, or `None` if the total weight is 0.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{Rng, WeightedTable};
let t = WeightedTable::new().with('a', 0.0).with('b', 1.0);
assert_eq!(t.pick_index(&mut Rng::new(0)), Some(1));
```

One item, or `None` if the total weight is 0.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{Rng, WeightedTable};
assert_eq!(WeightedTable::new().with("x", 1.0).pick(&mut Rng::new(0)), Some(&"x"));
```

How a cluster thins out from its center (`t = 0`) to its edge (`t = 1`).

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Falloff;
assert_eq!(Falloff::Linear.weight(0.0), 1.0);
assert_eq!(Falloff::Linear.weight(1.0), 0.0);
```

