Place `count` members round `center`, inside `radius`, with `falloff`.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{scatter_cluster, Falloff, Rng};
let kelp = scatter_cluster(&mut Rng::new(1), [10.0, 0.0], 4.0, 12, Falloff::Gaussian);
assert_eq!(kelp.len(), 12);
```

Place `per_cluster` members round each center. `ClusterMember::cluster`
tells which center a member belongs to.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{clusters, poisson_disc, Area, Falloff, Rng};
let world = Rng::new(8);
let area = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [100.0, 100.0]);
let centers = poisson_disc(&mut world.stream("reef centers"), area, 30.0);
let coral = clusters(&mut world.stream("reef coral"), &centers, 8.0, 15, Falloff::Smooth);
assert_eq!(coral.len(), centers.len() * 15);
```

How a prop roots into a surface.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::Rooting;
let r = Rooting { sink: 0.3, ..Rooting::default() };
assert_eq!(r.world_up, [0.0, 1.0]);
```

