items.doc:
The normal of a height function `y = height(x)` by central difference.
The normal points to `+y`.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::surface_normal;
let n = surface_normal(|_| 3.0, 1.0, 0.01);
assert!((n[1] - 1.0).abs() < 1e-5);
```

Root props at each `x` into a surface given as `surface(x) -> (y, normal)`.

Positions on slopes steeper than `rooting.max_slope_deg` get no prop.
The normal need not be unit length; it is turned to face `world_up`.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{place_on_surface, surface_normal, Rooting};
let ground = |x: f32| 5.0 + (x * 0.2).sin() * 2.0;
let props = place_on_surface(
(0..20).map(|i| i as f32 * 3.0),
|x| (ground(x), surface_normal(ground, x, 0.05)),
&Rooting::default(),
);
assert!(props.iter().all(|p| p.pos[1] <= ground(p.pos[0]) + 1.0));
```

A prop rooted on 3D ground. World up is `+y`.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{place_on_ground, Rooting};
let p = place_on_ground([[0.0, 0.0]], |_, _| (1.0, [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]), &Rooting::default());
assert_eq!(p[0].up, [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]);
```

Root props at each `[x, z]` into 3D ground given as
`ground(x, z) -> (y, normal)`. World up is `+y`; `rooting.world_up` is
not used.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{place_on_ground, Rooting};
let flat = |_x: f32, _z: f32| (0.0, [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]);
let p = place_on_ground([[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]], flat, &Rooting::default());
assert_eq!(p.len(), 2);
```

The rule for a fair start.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::FairStart;
let rule = FairStart { min_score: 0.6, ..FairStart::default() };
assert_eq!(rule.max_seeds, 64);
```

