items.doc:
The site with the highest score, and that score. NaN scores never win.
Returns `None` if there are no sites.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::best_start;
let (site, score) = best_start([[0.0, 0.0], [5.0, 1.0]], |p| p[0]).unwrap();
assert_eq!((site, score), ([5.0, 1.0], 5.0));
```

Try seeds from `first_seed` until one has a start site that scores at or
above `rule.min_score`.

`sites(seed)` makes the candidate start sites of a seed (for example,
Poisson-disc points over the open floor). `score(seed, site)` is the
game's own rule for a good start. Build the world inside these closures
from `Rng::new(seed)`, so the pick is the same on every run.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{fair_start, poisson_disc, Area, FairStart, Rng};
let area = Area::new([0.0, 0.0], [100.0, 100.0]);
let food = |seed: u64| poisson_disc(&mut Rng::new(seed).stream("food"), area, 25.0);
let pick = fair_start(
1000,
&FairStart { min_score: 0.0, max_seeds: 16 },
|seed| poisson_disc(&mut Rng::new(seed).stream("starts"), area, 20.0),
|seed, site| {
// Score: closer food is better.
let near = food(seed).iter()
.map(|f| ((f[0] - site[0]).powi(2) + (f[1] - site[1]).powi(2)).sqrt())
.fold(f32::MAX, f32::min);
1.0 - near / 100.0
},
).expect("a fair start");
assert!(pick.score >= 0.0);
```

The score distribution over many seeds. NaN scores count as
negative infinity. With no seeds, every number is 0.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::score_seeds;
let r = score_seeds(0..100, |seed| (seed % 10) as f32 / 10.0);
assert_eq!(r.count, 100);
assert!(r.pass_rate(0.5) > 0.4);
println!("{r}");
```

Score each seed and return the distribution. Use it in a `#[test]` to
prove that most seeds give a fair world.

```
use warp_sdk::procgen::{score_seeds, Rng};
let r = score_seeds(0..50, |seed| Rng::new(seed).stream("start").f32());
assert!(r.min >= 0.0 && r.max < 1.0);
```

The fraction of seeds that score at or above `threshold`.

```
let r = warp_sdk::procgen::score_seeds([1, 2], |s| s as f32);
assert_eq!(r.pass_rate(2.0), 0.5);
```

The seeds that score below `threshold`.

```
let r = warp_sdk::procgen::score_seeds([1, 2, 3], |s| s as f32);
assert_eq!(r.failing(2.5), vec![1, 2]);
```

Counts in `bins` equal bins from `min` to `max`.

```
let r = warp_sdk::procgen::score_seeds(0..10, |s| s as f32);
assert_eq!(r.histogram(5).iter().sum::<u32>(), 10);
```

What the player must do to complete an objective.

```
use warp_sdk::quest::Target;
let t = Target::count(7, 5);        // counter 7 reaches 5
let r = Target::reach([1.0, 2.0, 0.0], 3.0);
assert_eq!(r.position(), Some([1.0, 2.0, 0.0]));
assert_eq!(t.position(), None);
```

