items.doc:
The objective state of one game: active, queued and completed objectives.

```
use warp_sdk::quest::{Objective, Target, Tracker};
let mut t = Tracker::new(vec![
Objective::new(1, 0, Target::discover(3, 1)).then(2),
Objective::new(2, 1, Target::survive(10.0)),
]);
t.start(1);
t.discover(3);
assert!(t.is_done(1));
assert!(t.is_active(2));
```

Starts objective `id`. Past the cap, the objective goes into the queue.
Returns false when the id is not in the book, or is already active,
queued or completed.

```
use warp_sdk::quest::{starter_chain, Target, Tracker};
let mut t = Tracker::new(starter_chain(1, [(0, Target::count(0, 1))]));
assert!(t.start(1));
assert!(!t.start(1));
```

The player is at `pos`. Completes `Reach` targets in range.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
t.set_position([0.0, 1.0, 0.0]);
```

The player brought `amount` of item `item` to place `to`.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
t.deliver(7, 9, 3);
```

The player found one thing of kind `kind`.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
t.discover(4);
```

`dt` seconds passed with the player alive. Advances `Survive` targets.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
t.tick(1.0 / 60.0);
```

Sets or clears a game flag. Branch conditions read the flags.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
t.set_flag(3, true);
assert!(t.flag(3));
```

True when the flag is set.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert!(!t.flag(3));
```

True when objective `id` is active (not queued).

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert!(!t.is_active(1));
```

True when objective `id` completed.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert!(!t.is_done(1));
```

The active objective ids, oldest first.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert!(t.active_ids().is_empty());
```

The queued objective ids, next first.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert!(t.queued_ids().is_empty());
```

Progress of objective `id` from 0 to 1. A completed objective gives 1.
An objective that is not active gives 0.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
assert_eq!(t.progress(1), 0.0);
```

One HUD row for each active objective, oldest first. No text.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
for v in t.views() {
let _ = (v.icon, v.progress, v.count, v.marker);
}
```

`(icon, position)` for each active objective that has a marker.

```
# let t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
for (icon, pos) in t.markers() { let _ = (icon, pos); }
```

Takes the events since the last call, oldest first.

```
# let mut t = warp_sdk::quest::Tracker::new(Vec::new());
let events = t.drain_events();
```

The state as bytes: flags, completed, active with progress, queue.
The book is not in the bytes. Events are not in the bytes.

```
use warp_sdk::quest::Tracker;
let t = Tracker::new(Vec::new());
let bytes = t.save();
let back = Tracker::load(Vec::new(), &bytes).unwrap();
```

A tracker over `book` with the state from [`Tracker::save`]. Ids that
are not in `book` drop from the active list and the queue.

```
use warp_sdk::quest::{starter_chain, Target, Tracker};
let book = starter_chain(1, [(0, Target::count(0, 3))]);
let mut t = Tracker::new(book.clone());
t.start(1);
t.add(0, 2);
let back = Tracker::load(book, &t.save()).unwrap();
assert_eq!(back.views()[0].count, (2, 3));
```

